#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:1
msgid "Batch rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **strongest** source of all: a row overrides the command line, "
"because in batch mode the command line describes the run and the row "
"describes this job. {doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/batch` is how batch "
"mode works; this page is its configuration view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:7
msgid "Column to option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:9
msgid ""
"Columns are matched case-insensitively, with spaces and underscores "
"equivalent — `save pdf`, `Save_PDF` and `SAVE PDF` are one column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "Column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`url`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`reports`, contributing the URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`reports`, one or more specifiers separated by `|`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`format`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`save pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`save_pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`target list`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md
msgid "`target_lists` — one element, taken whole"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:20
msgid ""
"Five columns, against sixteen options. That is the design, not an "
"omission: a batch row says what makes **this job** different, and "
"everything about the run as a whole — where the output goes, which "
"repository and database to use, how much parallelism, the output shape — "
"is said once on the command line or in a file rather than repeated on "
"every row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:25
msgid "Rules of a batch row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:26
msgid ""
"**An unknown column is an error**, not something ignored, and the message"
" names the column. Same principle as the file's unknown keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:29
msgid ""
"**Rows are numbered from one**, the header not counting, and every error "
"names its row. These files are edited in spreadsheets by people who will "
"never see a stack trace, and an error that cannot say which row is nearly"
" useless."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:33
msgid "**A header with no data rows produces no jobs**, which is not an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:35
msgid ""
"**`save pdf` is stricter here** than in the environment: literally `true`"
" or `false`, case-insensitively, and nothing else. A batch file is "
"written once and read by a program, not typed at a shell prompt, so the "
"permissiveness that helps a shell script buys nothing here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:39
msgid "How `url` and `pdf` combine in a row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:40
msgid ""
"The `pdf` cell is always split on the pipe, even when it holds one "
"element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:42
msgid ""
"**one element** is treated as the *singular* specifier, and a `url` in "
"the same row overrides its URL field. The two therefore can never "
"conflict — the common row is a URL in one column and a destination path "
"in the other;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:45
msgid ""
"**several elements** are a genuine plural, and a `url` alongside them "
"**is a conflict**, exactly as in the file and the environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/batch_rows.md:54
msgid ""
"The first row downloads to `local.pdf`; the second runs two named "
"documents as one job."
msgstr ""

